 "topic": "The ISS orbits Earth about every 90 minutes, so astronauts see 16 sunrises and 16 sunsets every 24 hours; the crew lives on a 24-hour day on GMT/UTC.",
 "sources": [
  "https://www.nasa.gov/international-space-station/space-station-facts-and-figures/",
  "https://science.nasa.gov/blogs/earth-matters/2016/01/15/sunrise-to-sunset",
